Manual Indent Summary

Outline,Context:
I want to create a new tab. Indent summary tab however manual.
The need for this is because after the ICRF, MEDIC, and Troop Lift sheet is out, I still need to make my own small little edits. Once I make the edits only then I would want to send the indent summary to the coylines. So I want to create a “Indent summary generator”. This indent generator tab should use files uploaded in dropbox to create an indent summary just like the indent summary tab however using the newly uploaded files that contain up to date ICRF MEDIC AND TROOP LIFT SHEETS.

Function Details:

1. Dropbox:
The user should be able to upload multiple files at once. Either by drag and drop or click the dropbox and selecting files. This tab will not reject or refrain from processing and outputting summary for dates out of the month (e.g. if there are indents inside the files for dates past the month it should still reflect/be included in the summary) however, changing the month should have a fresh memory of the indents. For example: if a user did not generate anything inside the month of november do not show any indent summaries on this tab. Once the user generates one summary, dont show the dropbox so big. Just give like an UPDATE INDENT SUMMARY BUTTON then can have popup for uploadpage/dropbox. 


2. ICRF:
It will be a xlsx file format will correspond to the icrf section’s sheet however please refer to the attached icrf file in this prompt. 
COMPANY is under 9-10 column reporting and destination. Take the company from there.

CONDUCT NAME column contains the name of the use. CONDUCT NAME can be derived from this column. Content will be something like: “SCH 2 - X COY - CONDUCT NAME” or it could be SCH 2 - CONDUCT NAME.” In both cases take the conduct name from here. 


DATE is in 4th and 6th column (start and end date), if certain indents have the same date and same conduct name.

Even if the conduct name only partially or doesnt match. If it is under same coy within the date and time duration of another conduct list it under that block of the summary. 

3. MEDIC ROSTER:
The user will upload a xlsx file. 
COY check company in coy column (column 3).
CONDUCT is under conduct column (column 6).
TIMING under timing column just show the starting time.

If within same date and time period please add on same conduct indent summary block.

4. TROOP LIFT SHEET or TROOP LIFT:


There should be two different ways the user should be able to upload this. One is an xlsx file and other is a long list text just copy paste from clipboard.
Troop Lift Sheet - It will be similar but some columns may get added or removed so just be cautious which column the app searches. The column that says “Day” (refer to the document to know where to see the column title) contains which day of the month (consider the month as the month the tab is on.
COY/UNIT column contains the coy initials (L, M, N or J and so on) as a single letter. Use the coy to check the coy first and then there should be a high key (if the naming is different must rely on the date) within the duration of the same day. 
TIME refer to time column (not time gap).
NO. OF BUSES there is also this number of buses column that must be found. Under here two things must be checked. If the number is non zero just in the indent summary the number of busses should just be that number. However, if it is 0 code must check the corresponding remarks section or tonners section to seek for other numbers that may represent the number of tonners. 

