Clarifications confirmed after reviewing the November example workbooks
-----------------------------------------------------------------------

- The Manual Indent Summary is a separate tab with the app's month navigation. Store generated results by school and month, shared with users of that school. A month with no generated result stays empty.
- Keep generated text read-only in the app, with per-company and copy-all buttons like the original Indent Summary. Do not provide line-by-line editing.
- Before a result exists for a month, show the upload/paste area. After generation, show an UPDATE INDENT SUMMARY button that opens the upload area.
- Detect the type of each uploaded workbook. When updating, replace the previously imported rows for each source type represented in the new upload, combine multiple newly uploaded files of that type, and de-duplicate repeated rows. Preserve source types that were not uploaded.
- Red-filled ICRF rows are cancelled. Exclude each cancelled row; keep a conduct if active rows or other valid indents remain, and omit it when no active indents remain.
- The ICRF example has Activity Name in column A, Reporting/Destination in I/J, and start/end date/time in E-H. Use Reporting/Destination to identify company, and Activity Name for conduct. Handle Excel-formatted date/time values and variable column positions where possible.
- The Medic example has Date, COY, Start Time, and Conduct columns. Use the selected app month for day-only dates. If a school-specific Medic row has a date/conduct but no company or time, retain it in the date-grouped To Be Determined section.
- Troop Lift XLSX imports should detect the Day, Time, COY/UNIT, Purpose, route, bus-count, remarks, and 5-ton support columns by header. When bus count is zero, inspect remarks/tonner fields for a tonner count.
- Troop Lift can also be pasted as a long, date-grouped text schedule (not as spreadsheet TSV). Parse the month title, date headings such as DD/MM, time or time range, route, bus/tonner quantity, and company/conduct clues in parentheses. Strip surrounding asterisks and ignore unrelated trailing notes. If the pasted schedule month differs from the selected app month, warn and block generation.
- Use the logged-in school as the strict scope for company summaries and shared saved data. Keep unmatched conduct details for a known in-scope company in that company's To Be Determined section; do not expose other schools' companies.
- Summary conduct headings show date(s) and conduct name without a time. Preserve the requested order: ammo, Medic, 5-ton prepark, 5-ton reporting, LUV, and Troop Lift. Use the detailed tab-separated Troop Lift layout; for IFC, group trips by date and phase (NMT, SITEST transition, RTU).
